I"<p>India speaks in hundreds of languages, and most of them are low-resourced for speech technology. We build datasets and models that respect this diversity: Boli, a multilingual dataset for understanding the stuttering experience; generative models that learn the vowel harmony of Assamese from raw audio; phonology-informed evaluation of multilingual text-to-speech; and, in a SERB-funded project, normative nasalance and acoustic characteristics of North-Eastern languages for language technology and speech therapy.</p>
